      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T18:48:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A quick update on this, I think the timing would be easier to get correct if we just directly request an Alert from the test instead of doing something to cause an Alert, like a power state change. \n\nJust trying this, sending Get_Status from the partner followed an Alert request, without any delay in between does cause a message discard in the unit test. The below test case failes without this CL, but passes with the CL and fully covers the added  \"else if\" condition. Meaning without the CL there is an unhandled message discard and one of the messages doesn\u0027t make it to the partner, and with the CL both messages get to the partner. \n\n\n    ZTEST_F(usb_attach_5v_3a_pd_source_rev3,\n            verify_recovery_on_alert_message_discard)\n    {\n        zassert_false(fixture-\u003esrc_ext.alert_received);\n        zassert_false(fixture-\u003esrc_ext.status_received);\n  \n        tcpci_partner_send_control_msg(\u0026fixture-\u003esource_5v_3a, PD_CTRL_GET_STATUS, 0);\n        zassert_equal(pd_broadcast_alert_msg(ADO_OTP_EVENT), EC_SUCCESS);\n\n        k_sleep(K_SECONDS(2));\n        zassert_true(fixture-\u003esrc_ext.alert_received);\n        zassert_true(fixture-\u003esrc_ext.status_received);\n    }\n\n\nBut, as you mentioned, without explicit synchronization this could be flaky. Plus, this would pass in a case where the message never gets discarded. So, I\u0027ll look at how to add a check for the message being discarded and add explicit synchronization to this test case before uploading the next patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "6d8094fe_8df7fbcf",
      "revId": "880bfec074c0e81fa0e46ec85c1e499565937434",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
